<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Flydubai pilot investigated over possible attempt to crash Tel Aviv-bound flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed522859fb4dbe428887eadb150e89b69fdc03236ca771dfc4660ca114da98a8</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flydubai-pilot-investigated-over-possible-attempt-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-flight/a-79484761--24ed602fb272.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flydubai-pilot-investigated-over-possible-attempt-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-flight/a-79484761?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Flydubai flight from the UAE to Israel made an emergency landing after one pilot stabbed another. Officials are investigating whether this was a deliberate attempt to crash the plane.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany raises Deutschlandticket price to €66.80 a month from 2027 under new cost-based formula</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24e066fb4048ae4bc1df1664119a73a8535eaace0d073aba0da0cd961339cc6c</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-raises-deutschlandticket-price-to-_66-80-a-month-from-2027-under-new-cost-based-formula/a-79492524--e67f73547557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-raises-deutschlandticket-price-to-€66-80-a-month-from-2027-under-new-cost-based-formula/a-79492524?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new cost-based formula has pushed up the price of Germany's nationwide public transport pass for 2027.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's nuclear program remains shrouded in mystery as the regime debates ditching non-proliferation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8b94c4b7d81b236c722bcd6134d4c03227bb35e1f7ca0da675c3272fd033411</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197--eb083345c8e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran's nuclear program is entering a critical phase as Tehran debates dropping out of a nuclear non-proliferation treaty. Satellite images also show activity at known nuclear sites.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Fullbright scholar imprisoned for 13 years in a Pakistani jail, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d881def575a8c7ce88d1fe5aece770a4dd00a378339205fc83a556466fbb33da</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-fullbright-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-in-a-pakistani-jail-is-hope/a-79490207--2eb272f62665.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-fullbright-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-in-a-pakistani-jail-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fullbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City Premier League charges: What do they mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2b4be4694f34226de860e5298969eeceba03fafccb9eb0f4eb6d4155c944660</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City have become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c326782d6b8c9fa708dc4ca5f3f8cb44ffffb5bff3909f6bb61bca770f58e03</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff at the Wiesn are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism. They're taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia elections: Polls overshadowed by exhaustion, exodus and geopolitics as ethnic politics eclipse real problems</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a5e4898ffd7faf559425db90dddeca15301d57dff2635fc87111f93bf2006fe</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-/a-79487802--91e658c381f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-real-problems/a-79487802?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia goes to the polls on October 4 to elect several parliaments and presidents. While voters worry about the economy and emigration, the campaign is focused on ethnicity, exposing the country's political paralysis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e4eb2420993afcf71f4621e0216bd03b1924b0890d4fc0cb202ed4a3bf40e01</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Eurovision remains marred by geopolitics: Ireland will boycott again because of Israel's participation. Still, the song contest is expanding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a36e45aba9eab808c68f3de0346f9215c1ed8ae319e8b6451923da0711ca629f</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eurovision-remains-marred-by-geopolitics-ireland-will-boycott-again-because-of-israel-s-participatio/a-79401752--b320a0475ab7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eurovision-remains-marred-by-geopolitics-ireland-will-boycott-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-still-the-song-contest-is-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea: Lost shark draws over half a million visitors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b91d57a894922ac32a663cd9155232174b34becfd108fc5b5a40996941e1bee5</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014--618815d2f667.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The South Korean port of Busan says that a stranded shark has become a major tourist draw. It's also named the ocean predator an honorary ambassador to the city.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Eiffel Tower chief Patrick Branco Ruivo to step down after female staff excluded during Hindu group's visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e5a6be1e8d9efc9cdb7d6dd30764cca658a30cbf8739f8c0781a4f3e2818550</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eiffel-tower-chief-patrick-branco-ruivo-to-step-down-after-female-staff-excluded-during-hindu-group-/a-79482406--4df26f6b2ddb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eiffel-tower-chief-patrick-branco-ruivo-to-step-down-after-female-staff-excluded-during-hindu-group-s-visit/a-79482406?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An investigation found management failures led to female Eiffel Tower staff being excluded during a Hindu group's visit.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Key opposition leaders meet to discuss poll body row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ddb18e715bb6bea9be957131322478576bd9ddb4b322865a44d64105e1e6822</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-key-opposition-leaders-meet-to-discuss-poll-body-row/live-79481549--3920f917ca04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-key-opposition-leaders-meet-to-discuss-poll-body-row/live-79481549?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's opposition leaders meet in New Delhi to push back against voter roll revisions and discuss poll body chief Gyanesh Kumar. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Cabinet approves care reform bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4484ad54224d5d8a966179ae702c874d211b9f6a93662006fced9cdc9ebd04a</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-cabinet-approves-care-reform-bill/live-79481802--240e37d04c9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-cabinet-approves-care-reform-bill/live-79481802?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German Cabinet has approved a draft bill on reforming the care system after long debate. Police have launched raids across Germany targeting Hells Angels gangs and a money-laundering network. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino is a 'postcard from the future' — and could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44443d37f3c60f5563e548f04b93f8a43c8abdaaaaea4f436c48c64d7a688be3</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945--e1a2336874a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The current El Nino could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths. Researchers warn it offers a glimpse of temperatures that may become normal within 20 years.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>US troops exit Iraq after more than a decade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2c8c3d23e3d14d9b19a15cb2dbecc7fb1694508c1ca27e3856de27050acb8e4</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-troops-exit-iraq-after-more-than-a-decade/a-79481523--a29aac3edc39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-troops-exit-iraq-after-more-than-a-decade/a-79481523?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The current deployment began in 2014 in an effort to combat 'Islamic State' extremists. Iran, which has sought a complete removal of the US military from the Middle East, celebrated the withdrawal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Alternative Nobel' honors women's rights activists, AI researcher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:498afb219eb315aafc87d8eddeef09ed6a98d91f9fc7754151a4b6d11e39208c</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alternative-nobel-honors-women-s-rights-activists-ai-researcher/a-79481171--13d01235661c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alternative-nobel-honors-women-s-rights-activists-ai-researcher/a-79481171?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Right Livelihood Award has gone to a female AI researcher and women fighting repression. The Sweden-based prize has been dubbed an "alternative Nobel."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary's reckoning with Orban's corrupt system picks up speed with high-profile arrests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:711466ecb36b62f145c2bfa119af6fc26514ae09d14876e68fe7e61c5629090c</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T04:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed-with-high-profile-arrests/a-79473714--21394904d7e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed-with-high-profile-arrests/a-79473714?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's Prime Minister Peter Magyar vowed to dismantle Orban's corrupt networks. High-profile figures are being arrested and many Hungarians are pushing for swift accountability, but the rule of law takes time.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea denies South's claim, calls DMZ blast a 'farce'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0279816f401ead007eb30fa6266fa6d628feaa7978096c9ac1d5317dac453f07</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T04:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-denies-south-s-claim-calls-dmz-blast-a-farce/a-79481164--66024b7f40bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-denies-south-s-claim-calls-dmz-blast-a-farce/a-79481164?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korean leader Kim Jong Un's sister Kim Yo Jong has accused Seoul of conspiracy after it blamed Pyongyang for the blast in the DMZ.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says AI companies agree to 'self-police'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c195f014c2a47f45cc3c4421082937186e4354443a890aaac6745bd798a40cc</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T23:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-says-ai-companies-agree-to-self-police/a-79480781--d32630472f25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-says-ai-companies-agree-to-self-police/a-79480781?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump said the US won't "stifle" the development of AI, which he sees as "bigger than the Industrial Revolution." The agreement comes amid mounting concerns over AI safety after recent hacking incidents.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco: King appoints first woman prime minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:049b8105bac091095ea4576c33ef137ca3b7a150f36e9fd70236106cb4692fe0</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T19:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister/a-79479722--c33d994c4432.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-king-appoints-first-woman-prime-minister/a-79479722?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The appointment of Fatima Zahra Mansouri comes after her center-right party won last week's parliamentary elections in Morocco. She had previously served as mayor of the city of Marrakesh.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Estonia blames Russia for arson attack on defense company</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc3e1f8d52ec5409100d61086458168830d1529a16c548771a2f867d4cdbc109</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T18:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/estonia-blames-russia-for-arson-attack-on-defense-company/a-79478937--9c2db295ded0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/estonia-blames-russia-for-arson-attack-on-defense-company/a-79478937?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Estonian government accused Moscow of an "act of sabotage" that is part of Russia's broader campaign across Europe. The Baltic state has received support from EU and NATO leaders.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
